  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inside Justice: Empowering human rights defenders in addressing domestic violence against women in Sri Lanka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Overall Objective&lt;/strong&gt; of this 24 months Action is to empower women and men human rights defenders (HRDs) and rights holders to address domestic violence (DV) and thereby encourage women&#xbf;s active leadership and productive engagement in civic spaces without the fear of stigma, intimidation or violence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Action entails three main &lt;strong&gt;Outcomes&lt;/strong&gt; :&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Outcome 1: Human rights defenders (HRDs) are empowered and protected to respond confidently and collectively to address domestic violence (DV).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Outcome 2: Rights holders are aware of their basic rights and are supported by HRDs to take positive action towards claiming these rights through available remedies and support services for domestic violence at the community level.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Outcome 3: Civic space is informed with timely and accurate knowledge to influence progressive structural change and accountability for cases of domestic violence at the national level.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
